IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `colc-common`
IMPORT `colc-concessions`
IMPORT `colc-levy`
IMPORT `colc-vehicles`

-- South Australian concessions switched on by a Commonwealth card or payment -- the concession holder's seat.
--
-- SEAT: the concession holder -- a holder of a Commonwealth concession card, a recipient of a listed Commonwealth
-- payment, or a low income earner, who owns or rents a home or owns a car. "Am I entitled to the cost of living
-- concession this year, and how much? By when must I apply? Do I get a water rates remission? How much of the
-- emergency services levy on my home is remitted? What comes off my car registration and my driver's licence?"
-- Every question is phrased as that person would ask it, on facts that person could state. The rules are in
-- colc-concessions.l4 (Cost of Living Concessions Act 1986 and Regulations 2020), colc-levy.l4 (Emergency Services
-- Funding Act 1998 and Remissions--Land Regulations 2014) and colc-vehicles.l4 (Motor Vehicles Act 1959 and Regulations
-- 2010); this module builds their records from plain answers and restates no rule. The Minister, the Commissioner of
-- State Taxation and the Registrar of Motor Vehicles appear only as what they mean for the holder.
--
-- Inputs with the same name mean the same fact in every question, so the form can ask each once.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website (State of South Australia, CC BY 4.0), taken
-- from the Open Australian Legal Corpus (CC BY 4.0); each text is as at the corpus scrape and may be out of date.
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice.
-- See NOTES.md.

§ `South Australian concessions -- the concession holder's questions`

§§ `The cost of living concession (Cost of Living Concessions Act 1986, ss 2, 3; Regulations 2020, regs 3, 4, 6-8)`

GIVEN `on 1 July my home was occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on 1 July my home was my principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `how I occupy my home` IS A `Capacity of occupation`
GIVETH AN `Occupation of premises`
`my occupation from my answers` `on 1 July my home was occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes` `on 1 July my home was my principal place of residence` `how I occupy my home` MEANS
    `Occupation of premises` WITH
        `the premises are occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes` IS `on 1 July my home was occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes`
        `the premises are the person's principal place of residence`             IS `on 1 July my home was my principal place of residence`
        `the capacity`                                                           IS `how I occupy my home`

@export Do I occupy my home as an owner, as a tenant, or neither, for the cost of living concession (Cost of Living Concessions Act 1986 s 2(2), (3), Regulations reg 4)?
GIVEN `on 1 July my home was occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on 1 July of the financial year, your home was used solely or mainly as a place to live (not mainly as a shop, office or farm)
      `on 1 July my home was my principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on 1 July of the financial year, your home was your principal place of residence
      `how I occupy my home` IS A `Capacity of occupation` @desc How you hold or occupy your home: as an owner (freehold, Crown lease, buying by instalments, a life tenancy, a home unit company, a long lease, an approved aged persons housing scheme, a beneficiary, a residential park site), as an owner's spouse or domestic partner, as a tenant or other occupier (residential tenancy, residential park tenancy, rooming house, supported residential facility, an approved written agreement), or none of these
GIVETH A `Way of occupying`
DECIDE `Do I occupy my home as an owner or a tenant` IS
    `the way the person occupies the premises` (`my occupation from my answers` `on 1 July my home was occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes` `on 1 July my home was my principal place of residence` `how I occupy my home`)

GIVEN `on 1 July my home was occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on 1 July my home was my principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `how I occupy my home` IS A `Capacity of occupation`
      `my Commonwealth card or payment on 1 July` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment`
      `on 1 July I was a relevant asylum seeker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on 1 July I was eligible for a South Australian support package for people fleeing international conflict` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my income earned during the financial year` IS A NUMBER
      `the Minister's low income amount for my class of person` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Person on 1 July`
`my position on 1 July from my answers` `on 1 July my home was occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes` `on 1 July my home was my principal place of residence` `how I occupy my home` `my Commonwealth card or payment on 1 July` `on 1 July I was a relevant asylum seeker` `on 1 July I was eligible for a South Australian support package for people fleeing international conflict` `my income earned during the financial year` `the Minister's low income amount for my class of person` MEANS
    `Person on 1 July` WITH
        `occupation` IS `my occupation from my answers` `on 1 July my home was occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes` `on 1 July my home was my principal place of residence` `how I occupy my home`
        `card or payment` IS `my Commonwealth card or payment on 1 July`
        `is a relevant asylum seeker` IS `on 1 July I was a relevant asylum seeker`
        `is eligible for a South Australian support package for persons fleeing international conflict` IS `on 1 July I was eligible for a South Australian support package for people fleeing international conflict`
        `income earned during the financial year` IS `my income earned during the financial year`
        `the Minister's low income amount for the person's class` IS `the Minister's low income amount for my class of person`

@export Am I an eligible person for the South Australian cost of living concession for the financial year: on 1 July, did I live in my home as an owner or tenant and hold a qualifying card, payment or status (Cost of Living Concessions Act 1986 s 3(1), Regulations reg 6)?
GIVEN `on 1 July my home was occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on 1 July of the financial year, your home was used solely or mainly as a place to live (not mainly as a shop, office or farm)
      `on 1 July my home was my principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on 1 July of the financial year, your home was your principal place of residence
      `how I occupy my home` IS A `Capacity of occupation` @desc How you hold or occupy your home: as an owner (freehold, Crown lease, buying by instalments, a life tenancy, a home unit company, a long lease, an approved aged persons housing scheme, a beneficiary, a residential park site), as an owner's spouse or domestic partner, as a tenant or other occupier (residential tenancy, residential park tenancy, rooming house, supported residential facility, an approved written agreement), or none of these
      `my Commonwealth card or payment on 1 July` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment` @desc The Commonwealth concession card you held, or the Commonwealth payment you received, on 1 July of the financial year (choose one if you have several; "none of these" if none)
      `on 1 July I was a relevant asylum seeker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on 1 July, you were seeking recognition as a refugee and held, had applied for, or had held (with no other visa since) a bridging visa E, or were receiving Status Resolution Support Service support
      `on 1 July I was eligible for a South Australian support package for people fleeing international conflict` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on 1 July, you were eligible for a South Australian Government support package for people fleeing international conflict
      `my income earned during the financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc The income you earned during the financial year, in Australian dollars (used only for the low income earner class)
      `the Minister's low income amount for my class of person` IS A NUMBER @desc The income limit the Minister has published on the concessions website for your class of person for that financial year, in Australian dollars; enter 0 if you are not relying on being a low income earner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an eligible person for the cost of living concession` IF
    `the person is an eligible person for the financial year` (`my position on 1 July from my answers` `on 1 July my home was occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes` `on 1 July my home was my principal place of residence` `how I occupy my home` `my Commonwealth card or payment on 1 July` `on 1 July I was a relevant asylum seeker` `on 1 July I was eligible for a South Australian support package for people fleeing international conflict` `my income earned during the financial year` `the Minister's low income amount for my class of person`)

GIVEN `the financial year I am asking about begins in` IS A NUMBER
      `I applied to the Minister before 31 December` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was paid the concession last financial year for the same home` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has my bank account details` IS A BOOLEAN
      `someone else has been paid the concession this financial year for the same home` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person lives in the same room as me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has approved splitting the concession between us` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I entered the Switch for Solar program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the financial year in which I entered Switch for Solar begins in` IS A NUMBER
      `I was paid the concession for the year I entered Switch for Solar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has decided that exceptional circumstances lift the Switch for Solar bar for this year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Concession claim`
`my claim from my answers` `the financial year I am asking about begins in` `I applied to the Minister before 31 December` `I was paid the concession last financial year for the same home` `the Minister has my bank account details` `someone else has been paid the concession this financial year for the same home` `that person lives in the same room as me` `the Minister has approved splitting the concession between us` `I entered the Switch for Solar program` `the financial year in which I entered Switch for Solar begins in` `I was paid the concession for the year I entered Switch for Solar` `the Minister has decided that exceptional circumstances lift the Switch for Solar bar for this year` MEANS
    `Concession claim` WITH
        `the financial year begins in` IS `the financial year I am asking about begins in`
        `applied to the Minister before 31 December in the financial year` IS `I applied to the Minister before 31 December`
        `was paid the concession for the previous financial year for the same premises` IS `I was paid the concession last financial year for the same home`
        `the Minister has been provided with ADI account details for payment` IS `the Minister has my bank account details`
        `another eligible person has been paid for the financial year for the same premises` IS `someone else has been paid the concession this financial year for the same home`
        `that other eligible person is a resident in the same room` IS `that person lives in the same room as me`
        `the Minister has approved splitting the payment with the other eligible person` IS `the Minister has approved splitting the concession between us`
        `entered the Switch for Solar program` IS `I entered the Switch for Solar program`
        `the financial year in which the Switch for Solar program was entered begins in` IS `the financial year in which I entered Switch for Solar begins in`
        `received a payment for the financial year in which the Switch for Solar program was entered` IS `I was paid the concession for the year I entered Switch for Solar`
        `the Minister has determined that exceptional circumstances lift the Switch for Solar bar for this financial year` IS `the Minister has decided that exceptional circumstances lift the Switch for Solar bar for this year`

@export Am I entitled to the South Australian cost of living concession for the financial year, and if not, why not (Cost of Living Concessions Act 1986 s 3(2), Regulations reg 7)?
GIVEN `the financial year I am asking about begins in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the financial year begins on 1 July, such as 2024 for 2024/25 (the deposited regulations apply from 2024/25)
      `on 1 July my home was occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on 1 July of the financial year, your home was used solely or mainly as a place to live (not mainly as a shop, office or farm)
      `on 1 July my home was my principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on 1 July of the financial year, your home was your principal place of residence
      `how I occupy my home` IS A `Capacity of occupation` @desc How you hold or occupy your home: as an owner (freehold, Crown lease, buying by instalments, a life tenancy, a home unit company, a long lease, an approved aged persons housing scheme, a beneficiary, a residential park site), as an owner's spouse or domestic partner, as a tenant or other occupier (residential tenancy, residential park tenancy, rooming house, supported residential facility, an approved written agreement), or none of these
      `my Commonwealth card or payment on 1 July` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment` @desc The Commonwealth concession card you held, or the Commonwealth payment you received, on 1 July of the financial year (choose one if you have several; "none of these" if none)
      `on 1 July I was a relevant asylum seeker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on 1 July, you were seeking recognition as a refugee and held, had applied for, or had held (with no other visa since) a bridging visa E, or were receiving Status Resolution Support Service support
      `on 1 July I was eligible for a South Australian support package for people fleeing international conflict` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on 1 July, you were eligible for a South Australian Government support package for people fleeing international conflict
      `my income earned during the financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc The income you earned during the financial year, in Australian dollars (used only for the low income earner class)
      `the Minister's low income amount for my class of person` IS A NUMBER @desc The income limit the Minister has published on the concessions website for your class of person for that financial year, in Australian dollars; enter 0 if you are not relying on being a low income earner
      `I applied to the Minister before 31 December` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied to the Minister for the concession, in the form the Minister requires and with any documents asked for, on or before 30 December of the financial year
      `I was paid the concession last financial year for the same home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were paid the cost of living concession for the previous financial year for this same home (then you need not apply again)
      `the Minister has my bank account details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has your bank, building society or credit union account details so the concession can be paid by electronic transfer
      `someone else has been paid the concession this financial year for the same home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another eligible person has already been paid the concession for this financial year for the same home
      `that person lives in the same room as me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If someone else has been paid for the same premises: whether they are a resident in the same room as you (this matters only for a rooming house or supported residential facility resident)
      `the Minister has approved splitting the concession between us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has approved splitting the concession between you and the other eligible person or persons living at the same home
      `I entered the Switch for Solar program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have entered the State Government's Switch for Solar program for the installation of solar panels
      `the financial year in which I entered Switch for Solar begins in` IS A NUMBER @desc If you entered Switch for Solar: the calendar year in which that financial year began, such as 2022 for 2022/23 (enter 0 if you did not)
      `I was paid the concession for the year I entered Switch for Solar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you entered Switch for Solar: whether you were paid the cost of living concession for the financial year in which you entered it
      `the Minister has decided that exceptional circumstances lift the Switch for Solar bar for this year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has determined that, because of exceptional circumstances, the Switch for Solar bar does not apply to you for this financial year
GIVETH A `Concession entitlement`
DECIDE `Am I entitled to the cost of living concession` IS
    `the person's entitlement to the concession` (`my position on 1 July from my answers` `on 1 July my home was occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes` `on 1 July my home was my principal place of residence` `how I occupy my home` `my Commonwealth card or payment on 1 July` `on 1 July I was a relevant asylum seeker` `on 1 July I was eligible for a South Australian support package for people fleeing international conflict` `my income earned during the financial year` `the Minister's low income amount for my class of person`) (`my claim from my answers` `the financial year I am asking about begins in` `I applied to the Minister before 31 December` `I was paid the concession last financial year for the same home` `the Minister has my bank account details` `someone else has been paid the concession this financial year for the same home` `that person lives in the same room as me` `the Minister has approved splitting the concession between us` `I entered the Switch for Solar program` `the financial year in which I entered Switch for Solar begins in` `I was paid the concession for the year I entered Switch for Solar` `the Minister has decided that exceptional circumstances lift the Switch for Solar bar for this year`)

DECLARE `Dollar answer` IS ONE OF
    `the amount, in Australian dollars, is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered: the deposited regulations apply from the 2024/2025 financial year`

GIVEN `the financial year I am asking about begins in` IS A NUMBER
      `the Adelaide CPI for the December quarter before the financial year` IS A NUMBER
      `the Adelaide CPI for the December quarter of 2023` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Indexation figures`
`the indexation figures from my answers` `the financial year I am asking about begins in` `the Adelaide CPI for the December quarter before the financial year` `the Adelaide CPI for the December quarter of 2023` MEANS
    `Indexation figures` WITH
        `the financial year begins in` IS `the financial year I am asking about begins in`
        `the CPI for the December quarter of the year before the financial year begins` IS `the Adelaide CPI for the December quarter before the financial year`
        `the CPI for the December quarter of 2023` IS `the Adelaide CPI for the December quarter of 2023`

@export How much is the South Australian cost of living concession for the financial year, indexed by the Adelaide CPI and never less than last year's (Cost of Living Concessions Regulations 2020, regs 8, 3(3), 3(4))?
GIVEN `the financial year I am asking about begins in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the financial year begins on 1 July, such as 2024 for 2024/25 (the deposited regulations apply from 2024/25)
      `the Adelaide CPI for the December quarter before the financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc The ABS Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the December quarter of the calendar year before the financial year begins (for 2025/26, December quarter 2024); not used for 2024/25
      `the Adelaide CPI for the December quarter of 2023` IS A NUMBER @desc The ABS Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the December quarter of 2023; not used for 2024/25
      `last financial year's concession amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The cost of living concession amount paid for the previous financial year, in Australian dollars (the amount can never fall below it); enter 0 if you do not know, and the answer then leaves that floor out
GIVETH A `Dollar answer`
DECIDE `How much is the cost of living concession` IS
    IF `the deposited regulations cover the financial year beginning in` `the financial year I am asking about begins in`
    THEN `the amount, in Australian dollars, is` (`the concession amount for the financial year` (`the indexation figures from my answers` `the financial year I am asking about begins in` `the Adelaide CPI for the December quarter before the financial year` `the Adelaide CPI for the December quarter of 2023`) `last financial year's concession amount`)
    ELSE `not covered: the deposited regulations apply from the 2024/2025 financial year`

DECLARE `Application deadline` IS ONE OF
    `apply on or before` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `no application needed: I was paid last financial year for the same home`
    `not covered: the deposited regulations apply from the 2024/2025 financial year`

@export By what day must I apply for the South Australian cost of living concession for the financial year (Cost of Living Concessions Regulations 2020, reg 7(1)(a), (2))?
GIVEN `the financial year I am asking about begins in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the financial year begins on 1 July, such as 2024 for 2024/25 (the deposited regulations apply from 2024/25)
      `I was paid the concession last financial year for the same home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were paid the cost of living concession for the previous financial year for this same home (then you need not apply again)
GIVETH AN `Application deadline`
DECIDE `By what day must I apply for the cost of living concession` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the deposited regulations cover the financial year beginning in` `the financial year I am asking about begins in`)
            THEN `not covered: the deposited regulations apply from the 2024/2025 financial year`
        IF `I was paid the concession last financial year for the same home`
            THEN `no application needed: I was paid last financial year for the same home`
        OTHERWISE `apply on or before` (`the last day to apply for the concession for the financial year beginning in` `the financial year I am asking about begins in`)

DECLARE `Switch for Solar bar` IS ONE OF
    `barred for the financial years beginning in` HAS
        `the first` IS A NUMBER
        `the last` IS A NUMBER
    `not barred: I did not enter the Switch for Solar program`

-- (The Minister's reg 7(3c) exception is year by year; see `Am I entitled to the cost of living concession`.)
@export If I entered the Switch for Solar program, for which financial years am I barred from the cost of living concession (Cost of Living Concessions Regulations 2020, reg 7(3a))?
GIVEN `I entered the Switch for Solar program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have entered the State Government's Switch for Solar program for the installation of solar panels
      `the financial year in which I entered Switch for Solar begins in` IS A NUMBER @desc If you entered Switch for Solar: the calendar year in which that financial year began, such as 2022 for 2022/23 (enter 0 if you did not)
      `I was paid the concession for the year I entered Switch for Solar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you entered Switch for Solar: whether you were paid the cost of living concession for the financial year in which you entered it
GIVETH A `Switch for Solar bar`
DECIDE `For which years does Switch for Solar bar my concession` IS
    IF `I entered the Switch for Solar program`
    THEN `barred for the financial years beginning in` `the financial year in which I entered Switch for Solar begins in` (`the last financial year barred by Switch for Solar begins in` `my claim`)
    ELSE `not barred: I did not enter the Switch for Solar program`
    WHERE
        `my claim` MEANS `my claim from my answers` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `I entered the Switch for Solar program` `the financial year in which I entered Switch for Solar begins in` `I was paid the concession for the year I entered Switch for Solar` FALSE
        -- the claim fields other than the three Switch for Solar facts are not read by these rules: fixed placeholders.

§§ `If I was paid a concession I was not entitled to (Cost of Living Concessions Act 1986, ss 7, 8(2)-(4)) -- only if this has happened to you`

@export If I was paid a South Australian cost of living concession I was not entitled to, how much can the Minister recover from me as a debt (Cost of Living Concessions Act 1986 s 8(3)-(4), Regulations reg 7(3b))?
GIVEN `the concession amount I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the cost of living concession you were paid, in Australian dollars
      `I was entitled to that payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were in fact entitled to the payment (see the entitlement question)
      `I was paid it before entering Switch for Solar in the same financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the only reason you were not entitled is that you entered the Switch for Solar program in that financial year after you had been paid
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much can the Minister recover from me as a debt` IS
    `the amount recoverable as a debt due to the Minister` `the concession amount I was paid` `I was entitled to that payment` `I was paid it before entering Switch for Solar in the same financial year`

@export What is the most I can be fined for not telling the Minister in writing that I no longer meet a remission criterion, or for not telling the Minister of and refunding a cost of living payment I was not entitled to (Cost of Living Concessions Act 1986 s 8(2), (3))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined under section 8(2) or (3)` IS
    `the maximum penalty under section 8(2) or (3)`

@export If the Minister pays my cost of living concession late, is any interest paid to me (Cost of Living Concessions Act 1986 s 7(2))? The answer is the interest, in Australian dollars.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What interest is paid to me on a late concession` IS
    `the interest the Minister pays on a concession`

§§ `Water rates remission (Cost of Living Concessions Act 1986, s 4; Regulations 2020, reg 5) -- only if you pay irrigation rates`

GIVEN `how I occupy my home` IS A `Capacity of occupation`
      `my home was my principal place of residence on the dates I was billed and the rates were payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my spouse or domestic partner lives there as their principal place of residence too` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my Commonwealth card or payment when billed or payable` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment`
      `I held it on the date I was billed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I held it on the date the rates were payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my spouse or domestic partner's Commonwealth card or payment when billed or payable` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment`
      `my spouse or domestic partner held it on the date I was billed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my spouse or domestic partner held it on the date the rates were payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was entitled to the remission for the preceding rating period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied on a means test that I suffer exceptional hardship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my water rates for the financial year` IS A NUMBER
      `my share of my home` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Water rates position`
`my water rates position from my answers` `how I occupy my home` `my home was my principal place of residence on the dates I was billed and the rates were payable` `my spouse or domestic partner lives there as their principal place of residence too` `my Commonwealth card or payment when billed or payable` `I held it on the date I was billed` `I held it on the date the rates were payable` `my spouse or domestic partner's Commonwealth card or payment when billed or payable` `my spouse or domestic partner held it on the date I was billed` `my spouse or domestic partner held it on the date the rates were payable` `I was entitled to the remission for the preceding rating period` `the Minister is satisfied on a means test that I suffer exceptional hardship` `my water rates for the financial year` `my share of my home` MEANS
    `Water rates position` WITH
        `the water rates for the land for the financial year` IS `my water rates for the financial year`
        `the ratepayer's proportion of interest in the land` IS `my share of my home`
        `the ratepayer occupies the land as principal place of residence in a prescribed capacity` IS `the person occupies the land as principal place of residence in a prescribed capacity` `my occupation`
        `the spouse or domestic partner also occupies the land as principal place of residence` IS `my spouse or domestic partner lives there as their principal place of residence too`
        `the ratepayer holds a prescribed card or receives prescribed payments on the date billed` IS (`mine qualifies` AND `I held it on the date I was billed`)
        `the ratepayer holds a prescribed card or receives prescribed payments on the date payable` IS (`mine qualifies` AND `I held it on the date the rates were payable`)
        `the spouse or domestic partner holds a prescribed card or receives prescribed payments on the date billed` IS (`spouse's qualifies` AND `my spouse or domestic partner held it on the date I was billed`)
        `the spouse or domestic partner holds a prescribed card or receives prescribed payments on the date payable` IS (`spouse's qualifies` AND `my spouse or domestic partner held it on the date the rates were payable`)
        `the ratepayer was entitled to a remission of water rates for the preceding rating period` IS `I was entitled to the remission for the preceding rating period`
        `the Minister is satisfied by a means test that the ratepayer suffers exceptional circumstances of hardship` IS `the Minister is satisfied on a means test that I suffer exceptional hardship`
    WHERE
        -- the residential-purposes field is not read by the reg 3(2) rule: fixed placeholder.
        `my occupation` MEANS `my occupation from my answers` TRUE `my home was my principal place of residence on the dates I was billed and the rates were payable` `how I occupy my home`
        `mine qualifies` MEANS `is a prescribed card or prescribed payments` `my Commonwealth card or payment when billed or payable`
        `spouse's qualifies` MEANS `is a prescribed card or prescribed payments` `my spouse or domestic partner's Commonwealth card or payment when billed or payable`

@export Do I meet the criteria for a remission of my water (irrigation) rates? If I do, I am entitled to it if the Minister is of the opinion that I meet them (Cost of Living Concessions Act 1986 s 4(3), Regulations reg 5(1), (2)).
GIVEN `how I occupy my home` IS A `Capacity of occupation` @desc How you hold or occupy your home: as an owner (freehold, Crown lease, buying by instalments, a life tenancy, a home unit company, a long lease, an approved aged persons housing scheme, a beneficiary, a residential park site), as an owner's spouse or domestic partner, as a tenant or other occupier (residential tenancy, residential park tenancy, rooming house, supported residential facility, an approved written agreement), or none of these
      `my home was my principal place of residence on the dates I was billed and the rates were payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land was your principal place of residence when you were billed with the water rates and when they were payable
      `my spouse or domestic partner lives there as their principal place of residence too` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or domestic partner also lives on the land as their principal place of residence (answer no if you have none)
      `my Commonwealth card or payment when billed or payable` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment` @desc The Commonwealth concession card you held, or Commonwealth payment you received, around the time you were billed and the rates were payable ("none of these" if none)
      `I held it on the date I was billed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you held that card or received that payment on the date you were billed with the water rates
      `I held it on the date the rates were payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you held that card or received that payment on the date the water rates were payable
      `my spouse or domestic partner's Commonwealth card or payment when billed or payable` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment` @desc The Commonwealth concession card your spouse or domestic partner held, or payment they received, around those dates ("none of these" if none, or if you have no spouse or partner)
      `my spouse or domestic partner held it on the date I was billed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or domestic partner held that card or payment on the date you were billed
      `my spouse or domestic partner held it on the date the rates were payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or domestic partner held that card or payment on the date the rates were payable
      `I was entitled to the remission for the preceding rating period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were entitled to a water rates remission for the previous rating period, for this or other land
      `the Minister is satisfied on a means test that I suffer exceptional hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the rates are being recovered, the Minister is satisfied on the Minister's means test that you are suffering exceptional circumstances of hardship
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the criteria for a water rates remission` IF
    `the ratepayer meets the regulation 5 criteria for a remission of water rates` (`my water rates position from my answers` `how I occupy my home` `my home was my principal place of residence on the dates I was billed and the rates were payable` `my spouse or domestic partner lives there as their principal place of residence too` `my Commonwealth card or payment when billed or payable` `I held it on the date I was billed` `I held it on the date the rates were payable` `my spouse or domestic partner's Commonwealth card or payment when billed or payable` `my spouse or domestic partner held it on the date I was billed` `my spouse or domestic partner held it on the date the rates were payable` `I was entitled to the remission for the preceding rating period` `the Minister is satisfied on a means test that I suffer exceptional hardship` 0 1)
    -- the rates and the share (0 and 1) are not read by the criteria rule: fixed placeholders.

@export How much of my water (irrigation) rates for the financial year is remitted: 30% of the rates within the indexed minimum and maximum, in proportion to my share of the land (Cost of Living Concessions Regulations 2020, reg 5(3)-(5), reg 3(3)-(4))?
GIVEN `the financial year I am asking about begins in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the financial year begins on 1 July, such as 2024 for 2024/25 (the deposited regulations apply from 2024/25)
      `how I occupy my home` IS A `Capacity of occupation` @desc How you hold or occupy your home: as an owner (freehold, Crown lease, buying by instalments, a life tenancy, a home unit company, a long lease, an approved aged persons housing scheme, a beneficiary, a residential park site), as an owner's spouse or domestic partner, as a tenant or other occupier (residential tenancy, residential park tenancy, rooming house, supported residential facility, an approved written agreement), or none of these
      `my home was my principal place of residence on the dates I was billed and the rates were payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land was your principal place of residence when you were billed with the water rates and when they were payable
      `my spouse or domestic partner lives there as their principal place of residence too` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or domestic partner also lives on the land as their principal place of residence (answer no if you have none)
      `my Commonwealth card or payment when billed or payable` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment` @desc The Commonwealth concession card you held, or Commonwealth payment you received, around the time you were billed and the rates were payable ("none of these" if none)
      `I held it on the date I was billed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you held that card or received that payment on the date you were billed with the water rates
      `I held it on the date the rates were payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you held that card or received that payment on the date the water rates were payable
      `my spouse or domestic partner's Commonwealth card or payment when billed or payable` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment` @desc The Commonwealth concession card your spouse or domestic partner held, or payment they received, around those dates ("none of these" if none, or if you have no spouse or partner)
      `my spouse or domestic partner held it on the date I was billed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or domestic partner held that card or payment on the date you were billed
      `my spouse or domestic partner held it on the date the rates were payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or domestic partner held that card or payment on the date the rates were payable
      `I was entitled to the remission for the preceding rating period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were entitled to a water rates remission for the previous rating period, for this or other land
      `the Minister is satisfied on a means test that I suffer exceptional hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the rates are being recovered, the Minister is satisfied on the Minister's means test that you are suffering exceptional circumstances of hardship
      `my water rates for the financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc Your water rates for the land for the financial year, in Australian dollars: rates under the Irrigation Act 2009 or the Renmark Irrigation Trust Act 2009
      `my share of my home` IS A NUMBER @desc Your share of the land as a fraction from 0 to 1 (1 if you own it alone, 0.5 for a half share)
      `the Adelaide CPI for the December quarter before the financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc The ABS Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the December quarter of the calendar year before the financial year begins (for 2025/26, December quarter 2024); not used for 2024/25
      `the Adelaide CPI for the December quarter of 2023` IS A NUMBER @desc The ABS Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the December quarter of 2023; not used for 2024/25
      `last financial year's minimum water rates remission` IS A NUMBER @desc The prescribed minimum water rates remission for the previous financial year, in Australian dollars; enter 0 if you do not know, and the answer then leaves the reg 3(4) floor out
      `last financial year's maximum water rates remission` IS A NUMBER @desc The prescribed maximum water rates remission for the previous financial year, in Australian dollars; enter 0 if you do not know, and the answer then leaves the reg 3(4) floor out
GIVETH A `Dollar answer`
DECIDE `How much of my water rates is remitted` IS
    IF `the deposited regulations cover the financial year beginning in` `the financial year I am asking about begins in`
    THEN `the amount, in Australian dollars, is` (`the ratepayer's remission of water rates` `my position` `the minimum` `the maximum`)
    ELSE `not covered: the deposited regulations apply from the 2024/2025 financial year`
    WHERE
        `my position` MEANS `my water rates position from my answers` `how I occupy my home` `my home was my principal place of residence on the dates I was billed and the rates were payable` `my spouse or domestic partner lives there as their principal place of residence too` `my Commonwealth card or payment when billed or payable` `I held it on the date I was billed` `I held it on the date the rates were payable` `my spouse or domestic partner's Commonwealth card or payment when billed or payable` `my spouse or domestic partner held it on the date I was billed` `my spouse or domestic partner held it on the date the rates were payable` `I was entitled to the remission for the preceding rating period` `the Minister is satisfied on a means test that I suffer exceptional hardship` `my water rates for the financial year` `my share of my home`
        `the figures` MEANS `the indexation figures from my answers` `the financial year I am asking about begins in` `the Adelaide CPI for the December quarter before the financial year` `the Adelaide CPI for the December quarter of 2023`
        `the minimum` MEANS `the indexed amount` `the prescribed minimum remission stated in regulation 5(5)` `the figures` `last financial year's minimum water rates remission`
        `the maximum` MEANS `the indexed amount` `the prescribed maximum remission stated in regulation 5(5)` `the figures` `last financial year's maximum water rates remission`

§§ `The emergency services levy on my home (Emergency Services Funding Act 1998, ss 3, 15, 16; Remissions--Land Regulations 2014, regs 3, 5A, 6-8) -- only if you own your home`

GIVEN `the financial year I am asking about begins in` IS A NUMBER
      `the land use on my notice of levy is residential` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the levy on my notice` IS A NUMBER
      `the concession holders' remission for the whole land` IS A NUMBER
      `the general remission for the whole land` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Land under the notice of levy`
`my land from my answers` `the financial year I am asking about begins in` `the land use on my notice of levy is residential` `the levy on my notice` `the concession holders' remission for the whole land` `the general remission for the whole land` MEANS
    `Land under the notice of levy` WITH
        `the levy's financial year begins in` IS `the financial year I am asking about begins in`
        `the land is residential land` IS `the land use on my notice of levy is residential`
        `the amount of the levy` IS `the levy on my notice`
        `the regulation 7(2) remission for the land` IS `the concession holders' remission for the whole land`
        `the regulation 7(1a) remission for the land` IS `the general remission for the whole land`

-- A co-owning spouse or domestic partner is taken to hold the same kind of interest as the person asking.
GIVEN `my interest in my home at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July` IS AN `Interest in land`
      `my share of my home` IS A NUMBER
      `my Commonwealth card or payment during the levy notice period` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment`
      `I held it on the issue date, on the payment date, or at some time between` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied my home was my principal place of residence on 1 July` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my spouse or domestic partner co-owns my home` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my spouse or domestic partner's share of my home` IS A NUMBER
      `my spouse or domestic partner's Commonwealth card or payment during the levy notice period` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment`
      `my spouse or domestic partner held it on the issue date, on the payment date, or at some time between` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied my home was my spouse or domestic partner's principal place of residence on 1 July` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another co-owner of my home is entitled to the concession holders' remission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Owners of the home`
`the owners of my home from my answers` `my interest in my home at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July` `my share of my home` `my Commonwealth card or payment during the levy notice period` `I held it on the issue date, on the payment date, or at some time between` `the Minister is satisfied my home was my principal place of residence on 1 July` `my spouse or domestic partner co-owns my home` `my spouse or domestic partner's share of my home` `my spouse or domestic partner's Commonwealth card or payment during the levy notice period` `my spouse or domestic partner held it on the issue date, on the payment date, or at some time between` `the Minister is satisfied my home was my spouse or domestic partner's principal place of residence on 1 July` `another co-owner of my home is entitled to the concession holders' remission` MEANS
    `Owners of the home` WITH
        `the owner asking` IS `Owner of the home` WITH
            `interest at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July` IS `my interest in my home at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July`
            `share of the land` IS `my share of my home`
            `card or payment` IS `my Commonwealth card or payment during the levy notice period`
            `falls within a class on the date of issue, on the payment date or at any time between` IS `I held it on the issue date, on the payment date, or at some time between`
            `the Minister is satisfied the land was the principal place of residence on 1 July` IS `the Minister is satisfied my home was my principal place of residence on 1 July`
        `a spouse or domestic partner co-owns the land` IS `my spouse or domestic partner co-owns my home`
        `the spouse or domestic partner` IS `Owner of the home` WITH
            `interest at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July` IS `my interest in my home at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July`
            `share of the land` IS `my spouse or domestic partner's share of my home`
            `card or payment` IS `my spouse or domestic partner's Commonwealth card or payment during the levy notice period`
            `falls within a class on the date of issue, on the payment date or at any time between` IS `my spouse or domestic partner held it on the issue date, on the payment date, or at some time between`
            `the Minister is satisfied the land was the principal place of residence on 1 July` IS `the Minister is satisfied my home was my spouse or domestic partner's principal place of residence on 1 July`
        `another co-owner is entitled to the regulation 6 remission` IS `another co-owner of my home is entitled to the concession holders' remission`

@export Am I liable for the emergency services levy on my home, and for how much can the Commissioner of State Taxation look to me (Emergency Services Funding Act 1998 s 3(1) owner, s 15(1)-(2), joint and several)? The answer is in Australian dollars, 0 if I am not liable.
GIVEN `my interest in my home at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July` IS AN `Interest in land` @desc Your interest in the land at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July of the financial year: holder of the fee simple (freehold), holder of a life estate, holder of the fee simple subject to someone else's life estate, a person entitled to occupy Crown land under a lease, licence or agreement to purchase, a person entitled to occupy under a River Murray shack lease, or a tenant or other occupier with none of these
      `the levy on my notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the emergency services levy on the land, as stated in the notice of levy, in Australian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `For how much of the levy can the Commissioner look to me` IS
    `the most the Commissioner can recover from one owner` `the levy on my notice` (`Owner of the home` WITH
        `interest at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July` IS `my interest in my home at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July`
        `share of the land` IS 1
        `card or payment` IS `none of these`
        `falls within a class on the date of issue, on the payment date or at any time between` IS FALSE
        `the Minister is satisfied the land was the principal place of residence on 1 July` IS FALSE)
    -- share, card, window and residence are not read by the liability rule: fixed placeholders.

@export Is the payment date on my notice of emergency services levy at least 28 days after the notice was served on me, as the Act requires (Emergency Services Funding Act 1998 s 16(2)(d))?
GIVEN `the date my notice of levy was served on me` IS A DATE @desc The date the notice of levy was served on you (or on any co-owner, which counts as service on all), as YYYY-MM-DD
      `the payment date on my notice of levy` IS A DATE @desc The date stated in the notice by which the levy must be paid, as YYYY-MM-DD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my levy payment date at least 28 days after service` IF
    `the payment date is at least 28 days after the notice was served` `the date my notice of levy was served on me` `the payment date on my notice of levy`

@export Am I entitled to the concession holders' remission of the emergency services levy on my home for 2024/2025, in my own right or as one of a couple (Emergency Services Funding (Remissions--Land) Regulations 2014, reg 6)?
GIVEN `the financial year I am asking about begins in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the financial year begins on 1 July, such as 2024 for 2024/25 (the deposited levy remissions are for 2024/25 only)
      `the land use on my notice of levy is residential` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land use shown on your notice of levy is residential
      `my interest in my home at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July` IS AN `Interest in land` @desc Your interest in the land at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July of the financial year: holder of the fee simple (freehold), holder of a life estate, holder of the fee simple subject to someone else's life estate, a person entitled to occupy Crown land under a lease, licence or agreement to purchase, a person entitled to occupy under a River Murray shack lease, or a tenant or other occupier with none of these
      `my share of my home` IS A NUMBER @desc Your share of the land as a fraction from 0 to 1 (1 if you own it alone, 0.5 for a half share)
      `my Commonwealth card or payment during the levy notice period` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment` @desc The current Commonwealth concession card you held, or Commonwealth payment you received, around the issue and payment dates on your notice of levy ("none of these" if none)
      `I held it on the issue date, on the payment date, or at some time between` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you held that card or received that payment on the date of issue on your notice, on the payment date, or at any time between them
      `the Minister is satisfied my home was my principal place of residence on 1 July` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister is satisfied that the land was your principal place of residence on 1 July of the financial year
      `my spouse or domestic partner co-owns my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or domestic partner also owns the land with you (answer no if you have none)
      `my spouse or domestic partner's share of my home` IS A NUMBER @desc Your spouse or domestic partner's share of the land as a fraction from 0 to 1 (0 if they own none)
      `my spouse or domestic partner's Commonwealth card or payment during the levy notice period` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment` @desc The current Commonwealth concession card your spouse or domestic partner held, or payment they received, around the issue and payment dates ("none of these" if none)
      `my spouse or domestic partner held it on the issue date, on the payment date, or at some time between` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or domestic partner held that card or payment on the date of issue, on the payment date, or at any time between them
      `the Minister is satisfied my home was my spouse or domestic partner's principal place of residence on 1 July` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister is satisfied that the land was your spouse or domestic partner's principal place of residence on 1 July as well
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to the concession holders' levy remission` IF
    `the owner asking is entitled to the regulation 6 remission` (`my land from my answers` `the financial year I am asking about begins in` `the land use on my notice of levy is residential` 0 0 0) (`the owners of my home from my answers` `my interest in my home at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July` `my share of my home` `my Commonwealth card or payment during the levy notice period` `I held it on the issue date, on the payment date, or at some time between` `the Minister is satisfied my home was my principal place of residence on 1 July` `my spouse or domestic partner co-owns my home` `my spouse or domestic partner's share of my home` `my spouse or domestic partner's Commonwealth card or payment during the levy notice period` `my spouse or domestic partner held it on the issue date, on the payment date, or at some time between` `the Minister is satisfied my home was my spouse or domestic partner's principal place of residence on 1 July` FALSE)
    -- the levy amounts and the other co-owner's position are not read by the entitlement rule: fixed placeholders.

@export How much of the emergency services levy on my home is remitted for me (and for my spouse or domestic partner if they co-own it), under the concession holders' remission (reg 7(2) amount plus the further $46) or the general remission (Emergency Services Funding (Remissions--Land) Regulations 2014, regs 5A, 6, 7, 8)?
GIVEN `the financial year I am asking about begins in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the financial year begins on 1 July, such as 2024 for 2024/25 (the deposited levy remissions are for 2024/25 only)
      `the land use on my notice of levy is residential` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land use shown on your notice of levy is residential
      `the levy on my notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the emergency services levy on the land, as stated in the notice of levy, in Australian dollars
      `the concession holders' remission for the whole land` IS A NUMBER @desc The concession holders' remission for the whole land under reg 7(2), in Australian dollars, as your notice of levy or RevenueSA shows it (its formula is missing from the deposited text)
      `the general remission for the whole land` IS A NUMBER @desc The general remission for the whole land under reg 7(1a), in Australian dollars, as your notice of levy or RevenueSA shows it (its formula is missing from the deposited text)
      `my interest in my home at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July` IS AN `Interest in land` @desc Your interest in the land at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July of the financial year: holder of the fee simple (freehold), holder of a life estate, holder of the fee simple subject to someone else's life estate, a person entitled to occupy Crown land under a lease, licence or agreement to purchase, a person entitled to occupy under a River Murray shack lease, or a tenant or other occupier with none of these
      `my share of my home` IS A NUMBER @desc Your share of the land as a fraction from 0 to 1 (1 if you own it alone, 0.5 for a half share)
      `my Commonwealth card or payment during the levy notice period` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment` @desc The current Commonwealth concession card you held, or Commonwealth payment you received, around the issue and payment dates on your notice of levy ("none of these" if none)
      `I held it on the issue date, on the payment date, or at some time between` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you held that card or received that payment on the date of issue on your notice, on the payment date, or at any time between them
      `the Minister is satisfied my home was my principal place of residence on 1 July` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister is satisfied that the land was your principal place of residence on 1 July of the financial year
      `my spouse or domestic partner co-owns my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or domestic partner also owns the land with you (answer no if you have none)
      `my spouse or domestic partner's share of my home` IS A NUMBER @desc Your spouse or domestic partner's share of the land as a fraction from 0 to 1 (0 if they own none)
      `my spouse or domestic partner's Commonwealth card or payment during the levy notice period` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment` @desc The current Commonwealth concession card your spouse or domestic partner held, or payment they received, around the issue and payment dates ("none of these" if none)
      `my spouse or domestic partner held it on the issue date, on the payment date, or at some time between` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or domestic partner held that card or payment on the date of issue, on the payment date, or at any time between them
      `the Minister is satisfied my home was my spouse or domestic partner's principal place of residence on 1 July` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister is satisfied that the land was your spouse or domestic partner's principal place of residence on 1 July as well
      `another co-owner of my home is entitled to the concession holders' remission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any other co-owner of the land (not you or your spouse or partner) is entitled to the concession holders' remission
GIVETH A `Levy remission`
DECIDE `How much of the levy on my home is remitted for us` IS
    `the levy remitted for the owner asking and a co-owning spouse or partner` (`my land from my answers` `the financial year I am asking about begins in` `the land use on my notice of levy is residential` `the levy on my notice` `the concession holders' remission for the whole land` `the general remission for the whole land`) (`the owners of my home from my answers` `my interest in my home at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July` `my share of my home` `my Commonwealth card or payment during the levy notice period` `I held it on the issue date, on the payment date, or at some time between` `the Minister is satisfied my home was my principal place of residence on 1 July` `my spouse or domestic partner co-owns my home` `my spouse or domestic partner's share of my home` `my spouse or domestic partner's Commonwealth card or payment during the levy notice period` `my spouse or domestic partner held it on the issue date, on the payment date, or at some time between` `the Minister is satisfied my home was my spouse or domestic partner's principal place of residence on 1 July` `another co-owner of my home is entitled to the concession holders' remission`)

DECLARE `Levy share answer` IS ONE OF
    `our share of the levy after the remissions, in Australian dollars, is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `not liable for the levy: not the owner at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July`
    `not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why the levy question is not covered`

@export What is my share of the emergency services levy on my home after the remissions (with my spouse or domestic partner's share if they co-own it), as between the co-owners (Emergency Services Funding Act 1998 s 15(2), Remissions--Land Regulations 2014)?
GIVEN `the financial year I am asking about begins in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the financial year begins on 1 July, such as 2024 for 2024/25 (the deposited levy remissions are for 2024/25 only)
      `the land use on my notice of levy is residential` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land use shown on your notice of levy is residential
      `the levy on my notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the emergency services levy on the land, as stated in the notice of levy, in Australian dollars
      `the concession holders' remission for the whole land` IS A NUMBER @desc The concession holders' remission for the whole land under reg 7(2), in Australian dollars, as your notice of levy or RevenueSA shows it (its formula is missing from the deposited text)
      `the general remission for the whole land` IS A NUMBER @desc The general remission for the whole land under reg 7(1a), in Australian dollars, as your notice of levy or RevenueSA shows it (its formula is missing from the deposited text)
      `my interest in my home at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July` IS AN `Interest in land` @desc Your interest in the land at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July of the financial year: holder of the fee simple (freehold), holder of a life estate, holder of the fee simple subject to someone else's life estate, a person entitled to occupy Crown land under a lease, licence or agreement to purchase, a person entitled to occupy under a River Murray shack lease, or a tenant or other occupier with none of these
      `my share of my home` IS A NUMBER @desc Your share of the land as a fraction from 0 to 1 (1 if you own it alone, 0.5 for a half share)
      `my Commonwealth card or payment during the levy notice period` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment` @desc The current Commonwealth concession card you held, or Commonwealth payment you received, around the issue and payment dates on your notice of levy ("none of these" if none)
      `I held it on the issue date, on the payment date, or at some time between` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you held that card or received that payment on the date of issue on your notice, on the payment date, or at any time between them
      `the Minister is satisfied my home was my principal place of residence on 1 July` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister is satisfied that the land was your principal place of residence on 1 July of the financial year
      `my spouse or domestic partner co-owns my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or domestic partner also owns the land with you (answer no if you have none)
      `my spouse or domestic partner's share of my home` IS A NUMBER @desc Your spouse or domestic partner's share of the land as a fraction from 0 to 1 (0 if they own none)
      `my spouse or domestic partner's Commonwealth card or payment during the levy notice period` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment` @desc The current Commonwealth concession card your spouse or domestic partner held, or payment they received, around the issue and payment dates ("none of these" if none)
      `my spouse or domestic partner held it on the issue date, on the payment date, or at some time between` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or domestic partner held that card or payment on the date of issue, on the payment date, or at any time between them
      `the Minister is satisfied my home was my spouse or domestic partner's principal place of residence on 1 July` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister is satisfied that the land was your spouse or domestic partner's principal place of residence on 1 July as well
      `another co-owner of my home is entitled to the concession holders' remission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any other co-owner of the land (not you or your spouse or partner) is entitled to the concession holders' remission
GIVETH A `Levy share answer`
DECIDE `What is my share of the levy after the remissions` IS
    CONSIDER `the levy remitted for the owner asking and a co-owning spouse or partner` `my land` `my owners`
    WHEN `not covered` `why` THEN `not covered` `why`
    WHEN `no remission: not the owner at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July, so not liable for the levy` THEN `not liable for the levy: not the owner at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July`
    OTHERWISE `our share of the levy after the remissions, in Australian dollars, is` (`our share of the levy after the remissions` `my land` `my owners`)
    WHERE
        `my land` MEANS `my land from my answers` `the financial year I am asking about begins in` `the land use on my notice of levy is residential` `the levy on my notice` `the concession holders' remission for the whole land` `the general remission for the whole land`
        `my owners` MEANS `the owners of my home from my answers` `my interest in my home at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July` `my share of my home` `my Commonwealth card or payment during the levy notice period` `I held it on the issue date, on the payment date, or at some time between` `the Minister is satisfied my home was my principal place of residence on 1 July` `my spouse or domestic partner co-owns my home` `my spouse or domestic partner's share of my home` `my spouse or domestic partner's Commonwealth card or payment during the levy notice period` `my spouse or domestic partner held it on the issue date, on the payment date, or at some time between` `the Minister is satisfied my home was my spouse or domestic partner's principal place of residence on 1 July` `another co-owner of my home is entitled to the concession holders' remission`

§§ `My car's registration (Motor Vehicles Act 1959, ss 37A-40A; Regulations 2010, reg 77) -- only if you own a car or trailer`

GIVEN `my vehicle is a heavy vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am entitled, as a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card holder, to reduced public transport fares in South Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have been a member of a naval, military or air force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `as a result of that service I am` IS A `Result of service`
      `I have lost the use of one or both legs and so cannot ever use public transport` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am the parent or guardian of a child who has lost the use of one or both legs and so cannot ever use public transport` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my vehicle will be wholly or mainly used to transport me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my vehicle will be wholly or mainly used to transport that child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another of my vehicles already has the reduced fee under the same section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a reduced fee is payable for my vehicle under another provision of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Motor vehicle and owner`
`my vehicle from my answers` `my vehicle is a heavy vehicle` `I am entitled, as a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card holder, to reduced public transport fares in South Australia` `I have been a member of a naval, military or air force` `as a result of that service I am` `I have lost the use of one or both legs and so cannot ever use public transport` `I am the parent or guardian of a child who has lost the use of one or both legs and so cannot ever use public transport` `my vehicle will be wholly or mainly used to transport me` `my vehicle will be wholly or mainly used to transport that child` `another of my vehicles already has the reduced fee under the same section` `a reduced fee is payable for my vehicle under another provision of the Act` MEANS
    `Motor vehicle and owner` WITH
        `the vehicle is a heavy vehicle` IS `my vehicle is a heavy vehicle`
        `the owner is entitled, as the holder of a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card, to reduced public transport fares in this State` IS `I am entitled, as a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card holder, to reduced public transport fares in South Australia`
        `the owner has been a member of a naval, military or air force of Her Majesty` IS `I have been a member of a naval, military or air force`
        `as a result of that service the owner` IS `as a result of that service I am`
        `the owner, from the loss of the use of 1 or both legs, is permanently unable to use public transport` IS `I have lost the use of one or both legs and so cannot ever use public transport`
        `the owner is the parent or legal guardian of a child who, from the loss of the use of 1 or both legs, is permanently unable to use public transport` IS `I am the parent or guardian of a child who has lost the use of one or both legs and so cannot ever use public transport`
        `the vehicle will be wholly or mainly used for the transport of the owner` IS `my vehicle will be wholly or mainly used to transport me`
        `the vehicle will be wholly or mainly used for transporting the child` IS `my vehicle will be wholly or mainly used to transport that child`
        `another motor vehicle of the owner is already registered at a reduced fee under the same section` IS `another of my vehicles already has the reduced fee under the same section`
        `a reduced fee is payable for the vehicle under a provision of the Act other than sections 38 to 38B` IS `a reduced fee is payable for my vehicle under another provision of the Act`

@export Is the registration fee for my car reduced, and under which section: an incapacitated ex-service owner (s 38), a pensioner entitlement card holder (s 38A), or loss of the use of the legs or the carer of such a child (s 38B)? Each holds if the Registrar is satisfied by the evidence it requires (Motor Vehicles Act 1959 ss 37A-38B).
GIVEN `my vehicle is a heavy vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is a heavy vehicle (for example a truck or bus with a gross vehicle mass over 4.5 tonnes)
      `I am entitled, as a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card holder, to reduced public transport fares in South Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a pensioner entitlement card issued under Commonwealth law (such as a Pensioner Concession Card) and, as its holder, are entitled to travel on South Australian public transport at reduced fares
      `I have been a member of a naval, military or air force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been a member of a naval, military or air force of the Crown
      `as a result of that service I am` IS A `Result of service` @desc The result of that service for you: totally and permanently incapacitated; incapacitated totally or permanently but not both; blind; lost a leg or foot; receiving a repatriation pension at the total incapacity rate; receiving a locomotion impairment pension at 70% or more of that rate; or none of these
      `I have lost the use of one or both legs and so cannot ever use public transport` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, because you have lost the use of one or both legs, you are permanently unable to use public transport
      `I am the parent or guardian of a child who has lost the use of one or both legs and so cannot ever use public transport` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the parent or legal guardian of a child who, because of losing the use of one or both legs, is permanently unable to use public transport
      `my vehicle will be wholly or mainly used to transport me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, during the registration period, the vehicle will be used wholly or mainly to transport you
      `my vehicle will be wholly or mainly used to transport that child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, during the registration period, the vehicle will be used wholly or mainly to transport that child (answer no if there is no such child)
      `another of my vehicles already has the reduced fee under the same section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another motor vehicle you own is already registered at the reduced fee under the same section (only one vehicle per owner may have it)
      `a reduced fee is payable for my vehicle under another provision of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this vehicle already gets a reduced registration fee under another provision, such as the primary producer (s 34) or outer areas (s 37) reductions
GIVETH A `Registration concession`
DECIDE `Is my car registration fee reduced` IS
    `the registration concession for the vehicle` (`my vehicle from my answers` `my vehicle is a heavy vehicle` `I am entitled, as a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card holder, to reduced public transport fares in South Australia` `I have been a member of a naval, military or air force` `as a result of that service I am` `I have lost the use of one or both legs and so cannot ever use public transport` `I am the parent or guardian of a child who has lost the use of one or both legs and so cannot ever use public transport` `my vehicle will be wholly or mainly used to transport me` `my vehicle will be wholly or mainly used to transport that child` `another of my vehicles already has the reduced fee under the same section` `a reduced fee is payable for my vehicle under another provision of the Act`)

DECLARE `Registration fee answer` IS ONE OF
    `the registration fee, in Australian dollars, is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered: more than one of sections 38, 38A and 38B would apply`

@export What is the registration fee for my car after the reduction: 66.667% off under s 38, 50% off under s 38A or s 38B (Motor Vehicles Regulations 2010, reg 77(3), (4))?
GIVEN `my vehicle is a heavy vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is a heavy vehicle (for example a truck or bus with a gross vehicle mass over 4.5 tonnes)
      `I am entitled, as a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card holder, to reduced public transport fares in South Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a pensioner entitlement card issued under Commonwealth law (such as a Pensioner Concession Card) and, as its holder, are entitled to travel on South Australian public transport at reduced fares
      `I have been a member of a naval, military or air force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been a member of a naval, military or air force of the Crown
      `as a result of that service I am` IS A `Result of service` @desc The result of that service for you: totally and permanently incapacitated; incapacitated totally or permanently but not both; blind; lost a leg or foot; receiving a repatriation pension at the total incapacity rate; receiving a locomotion impairment pension at 70% or more of that rate; or none of these
      `I have lost the use of one or both legs and so cannot ever use public transport` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, because you have lost the use of one or both legs, you are permanently unable to use public transport
      `I am the parent or guardian of a child who has lost the use of one or both legs and so cannot ever use public transport` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the parent or legal guardian of a child who, because of losing the use of one or both legs, is permanently unable to use public transport
      `my vehicle will be wholly or mainly used to transport me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, during the registration period, the vehicle will be used wholly or mainly to transport you
      `my vehicle will be wholly or mainly used to transport that child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, during the registration period, the vehicle will be used wholly or mainly to transport that child (answer no if there is no such child)
      `another of my vehicles already has the reduced fee under the same section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another motor vehicle you own is already registered at the reduced fee under the same section (only one vehicle per owner may have it)
      `a reduced fee is payable for my vehicle under another provision of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this vehicle already gets a reduced registration fee under another provision, such as the primary producer (s 34) or outer areas (s 37) reductions
      `the prescribed registration fee for my vehicle` IS A NUMBER @desc The full prescribed registration fee for the vehicle for the registration period, in Australian dollars, before any reduction (from the Regulations' fee scale or the registration renewal notice)
GIVETH A `Registration fee answer`
DECIDE `What is my car registration fee after the reduction` IS
    CONSIDER `my concession`
    WHEN `not covered: more than one of sections 38, 38A and 38B would apply, and each excludes a vehicle with a reduced fee under another of them` THEN `not covered: more than one of sections 38, 38A and 38B would apply`
    OTHERWISE `the registration fee, in Australian dollars, is` (`the registration fee after the reduction` `my concession` `the prescribed registration fee for my vehicle`)
    WHERE
        `my concession` MEANS `the registration concession for the vehicle` (`my vehicle from my answers` `my vehicle is a heavy vehicle` `I am entitled, as a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card holder, to reduced public transport fares in South Australia` `I have been a member of a naval, military or air force` `as a result of that service I am` `I have lost the use of one or both legs and so cannot ever use public transport` `I am the parent or guardian of a child who has lost the use of one or both legs and so cannot ever use public transport` `my vehicle will be wholly or mainly used to transport me` `my vehicle will be wholly or mainly used to transport that child` `another of my vehicles already has the reduced fee under the same section` `a reduced fee is payable for my vehicle under another provision of the Act`)

@export What is the registration fee for my trailer: half the prescribed fee for one trailer used wholly or mainly for my personal use, if I am a pensioner entitlement card holder (Motor Vehicles Act 1959 s 38AB, Regulations reg 77(4))?
GIVEN `my trailer is a heavy vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trailer is a heavy vehicle (gross vehicle mass over 4.5 tonnes)
      `I am entitled, as a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card holder, to reduced public transport fares in South Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a pensioner entitlement card issued under Commonwealth law (such as a Pensioner Concession Card) and, as its holder, are entitled to travel on South Australian public transport at reduced fares
      `my trailer will be wholly or mainly for my personal use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, during the registration period, the trailer will be employed wholly or mainly in your personal use
      `another of my trailers already has the reduced fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another trailer you own is already registered at the reduced fee under s 38AB (only one trailer per owner may have it)
      `the prescribed registration fee for my trailer` IS A NUMBER @desc The full prescribed registration fee for the trailer for the registration period, in Australian dollars, before any reduction
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my trailer registration fee` IS
    `the trailer's registration fee after the reduction` (`Trailer and owner` WITH
        `the trailer is a heavy vehicle` IS `my trailer is a heavy vehicle`
        `the owner is entitled, as the holder of a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card, to reduced public transport fares in this State` IS `I am entitled, as a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card holder, to reduced public transport fares in South Australia`
        `the trailer will be wholly or mainly employed in the personal use of the owner` IS `my trailer will be wholly or mainly for my personal use`
        `another trailer of the owner is already registered at a reduced fee under section 38AB` IS `another of my trailers already has the reduced fee`) `the prescribed registration fee for my trailer`

DECLARE `Reduced registration after an event` IS ONE OF
    `the registration stays in force until the end of` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `the registration runs its term: subsection (3) does not reach this event`

@export If I die or stop owning my car (or trailer) while it is registered at a reduced fee, until what day does the registration stay in force unless the balance of the full fee is paid (Motor Vehicles Act 1959 ss 38(3), 38A(3), 38AB(3), 38B(3))?
GIVEN `what has happened` IS AN `Event during a reduced-fee registration` @desc What has happened during the reduced-fee registration: the registered owner died; the registered owner stopped owning the vehicle (sold or gave it away); the owner still owns it but stopped holding the card or meeting the conditions; or nothing has changed
      `the day it happened` IS A DATE @desc The date of the death, or the date ownership ended (or the date of the other change), as YYYY-MM-DD
GIVETH A `Reduced registration after an event`
DECIDE `Until what day does my reduced registration stay in force` IS
    IF `subsection (3) applies to the event` `what has happened`
    THEN `the registration stays in force until the end of` (`the day the reduced-fee registration becomes void unless the balance is paid` `the day it happened`)
    ELSE `the registration runs its term: subsection (3) does not reach this event`

@export How much is the balance of the registration fee that I (as registered owner or operator) may pay at any time while a reduced-fee registration is in force, after which the vehicle may be used as if fully paid (Motor Vehicles Act 1959 s 40)?
GIVEN `the prescribed registration fee for my vehicle` IS A NUMBER @desc The full prescribed registration fee for the vehicle for the registration period, in Australian dollars, before any reduction (from the Regulations' fee scale or the registration renewal notice)
      `the reduced registration fee I paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The reduced registration fee you paid for the same period, in Australian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is the balance of my registration fee` IS
    `the balance of the prescribed registration fee` `the prescribed registration fee for my vehicle` `the reduced registration fee I paid`

@export I registered my car at the full fee and became entitled to a reduction during the registration: can I get part of the fee back (Motor Vehicles Act 1959 s 40A)?
GIVEN `I paid the full prescribed registration fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle was registered on payment of the full prescribed registration fee
      `I became entitled to a reduction or exemption during the registration period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, during that registration period, you became entitled to a reduction of, or exemption from, registration fees (for example, by getting a pensioner entitlement card)
GIVETH A `Refund on becoming entitled`
DECIDE `Can I get part of my registration fee back` IS
    `the section 40A refund` `I paid the full prescribed registration fee` `I became entitled to a reduction or exemption during the registration period`

§§ `My driver's licence (Motor Vehicles Regulations 2010, Schedule 1 clause 22, reg 76(4)) -- only if you hold or are getting a licence`

GIVEN `as a result of service in a naval, military or air force I am` IS A `Result of service`
      `I am entitled, as a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card holder, to reduced public transport fares in South Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Licence applicant`
`me as a licence applicant` `as a result of service in a naval, military or air force I am` `I am entitled, as a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card holder, to reduced public transport fares in South Australia` MEANS
    `Licence applicant` WITH
        `as a result of service in a naval, military or air force of His Majesty the applicant` IS `as a result of service in a naval, military or air force I am`
        `the applicant is a pensioner entitlement card holder` IS `I am entitled, as a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card holder, to reduced public transport fares in South Australia`

@export What is the fee for my South Australian driver's licence for the period I am taking it for: $26 a year for a pensioner entitlement card holder or an eligible ex-service person, $53 a year otherwise, by quarters for part years (Motor Vehicles Regulations 2010, Schedule 1 clause 22(1), (2))? The administration fee is separate.
GIVEN `as a result of service in a naval, military or air force I am` IS A `Result of service` @desc The result for you of any service in a naval, military or air force of the Crown: totally and permanently incapacitated; incapacitated totally or permanently but not both; blind; lost a leg or foot; receiving a repatriation pension at the total incapacity rate; receiving a locomotion impairment pension at 70% or more of that rate; or none of these, or no such service
      `I am entitled, as a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card holder, to reduced public transport fares in South Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a pensioner entitlement card issued under Commonwealth law (such as a Pensioner Concession Card) and, as its holder, are entitled to travel on South Australian public transport at reduced fares
      `the months the licence is for` IS A NUMBER @desc The length of the licence you are taking out or renewing, in months (12 for one year, 120 for ten years)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my driver's licence fee` IS
    `the driver's licence fee for the period` (`me as a licence applicant` `as a result of service in a naval, military or air force I am` `I am entitled, as a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card holder, to reduced public transport fares in South Australia`) `the months the licence is for`

@export What administration fee is payable on top of the licence fee when I get or renew my driver's licence (Motor Vehicles Regulations 2010, Schedule 1 clauses 1, 22(5))? The answer is in Australian dollars.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the licence administration fee` IS
    `the administration fee for the issue or renewal of a driver's licence`

@export If I stop being a pensioner entitlement card holder, what additional driver's licence fee must I pay for the rest of my licence: the full-fee difference for each complete 3 months left (Motor Vehicles Regulations 2010, Schedule 1 clause 22(3), (4))?
GIVEN `as a result of service in a naval, military or air force I am` IS A `Result of service` @desc The result for you of any service in a naval, military or air force of the Crown: totally and permanently incapacitated; incapacitated totally or permanently but not both; blind; lost a leg or foot; receiving a repatriation pension at the total incapacity rate; receiving a locomotion impairment pension at 70% or more of that rate; or none of these, or no such service
      `my licence was issued or renewed at the pensioner's reduced fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your current licence was issued or renewed on payment of the reduced fee for a pensioner entitlement card holder
      `the day I stopped being a card holder` IS A DATE @desc The date you stopped holding the card, or stopped being entitled as its holder to reduced public transport fares, as YYYY-MM-DD
      `my licence's expiry date` IS A DATE @desc The expiry date shown on your driver's licence (the last day it is in force), as YYYY-MM-DD
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What additional licence fee must I pay on losing my card` IS
    `the additional licence fee on ceasing to be a card holder` (`me as a licence applicant` `as a result of service in a naval, military or air force I am` FALSE) `my licence was issued or renewed at the pensioner's reduced fee` `the day I stopped being a card holder` `my licence's expiry date`
    -- after ceasing, the applicant is no longer a card holder: the card field is FALSE (it is not read by the clause 22(3) rule).

@export Does the time the Registrar's notice gives me to pay the additional licence fee meet the minimum of 14 days (Motor Vehicles Regulations 2010, reg 76(4))?
GIVEN `the days the Registrar's notice gives me to pay` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days, from the day the notice was given, that the Registrar's written notice allows you to pay the additional licence fee
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Registrar's notice give me enough time` IF
    `the Registrar's notice allows enough time` `the days the Registrar's notice gives me to pay`
